{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And Israel dwelt in the land of Egypt, etc.</b> One needs to know why it repeated saying ״בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם בְּאֶרֶץ גֹּשֶׁן״? <b>Further,</b> what connection and relevance does ״וַיִּפְרוּ״ etc. have with ״וַיֵּשֶׁב יִשְׂרָאֵל״?" "<b>Indeed,</b> the verse may be explained according to what we wrote on the verse (Genesis 46:3) ״כִּי לְגוֹי גָּדוֹל״ etc., for the cause of the descent to Egypt is to elevate the holy sparks that had been scattered and came there. And this is what it means by <b>And Israel dwelt in the land of Egypt</b> — meaning that it is a place of impure klippah — <b>in the land of Goshen</b>, from the root of drawing near (הַגָּשָׁה), for there were drawn together all the holy sparks through the agency of the branch of holiness, which is Israel, which is in the aspect of a drawing-stone for that which resembles it. And it used the singular form (וַיֵּשֶׁב) as an allusion to their being all of one unified heart with no separation among them, and through this <b>they laid hold of it</b> — meaning they grasped something in it, and those are the aforementioned sparks. And with this <b>they were fruitful and multiplied</b>, for as the souls multiply, those born multiply. And see what the Maggid of Maharik explained on the verse (Exodus 1:6) ״וַיָּמָת יוֹסֵף וְגוֹ׳ וּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל פָּרוּ וַיִּשְׁרְצוּ וַיִּרְבּוּ״, and you will find support for our words — the words of the living Elohim." "<b>Thus concludes the parashah of Vayigash.</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {1 "The phrase 'המגיד למהרי״ק' (the Maggid of Maharik) is uncertain in its reference; translated literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:49:44.282663114Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}